From 8a517694b1a453b2c9f212ebbd189e3d7236eb04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: machuanhu <1748771273@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 18:31:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(distributed): add unified_comm communication abstraction
 layer

- introduce vllm/distributed/unified_comm/ subpackage providing a
  device-agnostic, layered communication abstraction:
  Layer 1 CommBackend (NCCL/HCCL adapters), Layer 2 CollectiveOps,
  Layer 3 TransferPlane, Layer 4 CommStrategy
- new entry points: UnifiedCommAdapter and is_unified_comm_enabled
- HCCL backend supports two execution modes selectable via env:
  Mode A (default, torch.distributed) and Mode B (direct libhccl.so
  via pyhccl_wrapper, gated by UNIFIED_COMM_USE_DIRECT_HCCL=1)
- NCCL backend symmetrically supports Mode A / Mode B
- the layer is strictly opt-in: nothing in this commit changes the
  default code path; activation requires UNIFIED_COMM_ENABLED=1 in
  the environment
- README.md documents the architecture, integration model, env
  variables, and extension points

This commit only adds the new package. The integration into
GroupCoordinator and the smoke tests live in follow-up commits to
keep the diff reviewable.

Signed-off-by: machuanhu <1748771273@qq.com>
